{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U1", "U2"],
      "pins": ["U1.5", "U1.6", "U2.26", "U2.27", "U2.1", "U2.2", "U2.3", "U2.4", "U2.5", "U2.24"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC"],
      "observed": "The INA219 (U1) has A0/A1 strapped to GND (note 'I2C address: 0x40') and its SCL/SDA are on I2C2_SCL_FCC / I2C2_SDA_FCC. The PCA9685 (U2) has its address pins A0–A5 strapped to GND (giving 0x40) and its SCL/SDA (pins 26/27) are on the SAME I2C2_SCL_FCC / I2C2_SDA_FCC bus. Two devices therefore sit on one bus at the identical 7-bit address 0x40.",
      "expected": "A single I2C bus cannot host two devices at the same address. The U2 block's own annotation 'I2C address: 0x4x' indicates the address pins are meant to be strapped to a non-colliding value (or the PWM driver placed on a different bus) so that the FCC can address both the current sensor and the servo driver.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet: U1 INA219AIDCNR 'I2C address: 0x40', pin5 SCL -> I2C2_SCL_FCC, pin6 SDA -> I2C2_SDA_FCC"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U2 PCA9685PW 'I2C address: 0x4x', pin26 SCL -> I2C2_SCL_FCC, pin27 SDA -> I2C2_SDA_FCC, A0–A5 strapped to GND"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Component Table: 'PCA9685PW ... I2C addr 0x40' and 'INA219AIDCNR, I2C addr 0x40'"}
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC cannot distinguish the INA219 from the PCA9685 on I2C2; one of the two (current/voltage sensing or the 16-channel servo PWM) will not respond correctly, breaking power telemetry or servo control.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R49"],
      "pins": ["R49.1", "R49.2"],
      "nets": ["UART2_TX_FCC", "UART2_RX_NAVC"],
      "observed": "In the Connections sheet 'UART Connections' block, R48 (UART2_RX_FCC <-> UART2_TX_NAVC) is given the value 10, but the series resistor R49 (UART2_TX_FCC <-> UART2_RX_NAVC) has an empty value field.",
      "expected": "Every placed two-terminal passive must carry a value for assembly; the symmetric series resistor on the UART2 pair should be specified (10 Ω like R48, or 0 Ω).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Connections sheet, UART Connections: 'R48 10' on the top resistor, 'R49' with no value on the bottom resistor"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "TL;DR: 'NAVC↔FCC run UART2 + I2C + GPIO between the two MCUs'"}
      ],
      "impact": "With no value, the assembler may leave R49 unpopulated, opening the FCC→NAVC UART2 path and breaking the navigation-solution link between the two MCUs.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build matches the spec on part identities and most values, but it places the INA219 and the PCA9685 at the same I2C address (0x40) on the same I2C2_FCC bus, which the PCA9685's own '0x4x' annotation implies should not happen, and it leaves the UART2 series resistor R49 without a value; the address collision is the most consequential deviation."
}

